omoting these  dangerous behaviors that can trigger a  lifetime struggle with food I would also  argue that there's actual pro-ana  content floating around the app  juxtaposed against a number of eating  disorder recovery accounts as well now  while I'm all for helping young people  find a community to help them through  recovery  sometimes even seeing this kind of  content can be triggering for a lot of  people who are actively struggling for  example some recovery videos I saw gifts  civic numbers or weights and give body  checks which can be really triggering  for people who are actively struggling  with their disorders again there just  isn't enough time for nuance and context  in these videos they're really just  given you the polished highlight reel of  what recovery can look like I also do  worry that the apps algorithm might be  really dangerous for this population as  just after I watched a few of these  weight loss what I in a day videos I was  fed a ton of more problematic weight  loss and assorted lis content now I went  through tic TOCs Community Guidelines  and there were actually a few terms that  definitely could deem these videos as  being against the Community Guidelines  so for one they actually say that they  do not permit misinformation that may  cause harm to an individual's health and  two they also do say that they do not  permit any normalizing or encouraging of  triggering self-harm behavior including  content that supports pro-ana or other  dangerous behaviors to lose weight I  know that diet culture has us thinking  that eating less than a thousand  calories is normal or even a healthy  behavior for weight loss but I would  flag all five of these videos as  violating tick-tocks Terms of Use tick  tock  I mean reach out to me or really any  other health professional if you need  some help identifying what is  problematic and what is not because  there is a lot of content on the  platform that needs to come down I just  want to finish here 